<title>BELGIUM: Belgian car registrations up 3.7% yr/yr in Jan. [CORRECTED 12:35 GMT]</title>
<headline>Belgian car registrations up 3.7% yr/yr in Jan. [CORRECTED 12:35 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects dateline from Jan 4 to Feb 4.)</p>
<p>Belgian new car registrations rose 3.7 percent in January compared with the same year ago period, according to figures from the Belgian Federation of Automobile Manufacturers (Febiac).</p>
<p>    BELGIAN CAR REGISTRATIONS Jan 97	  Jan 96</p>
<p>    Month			   44,465	  42,873</p>
<p>The following manufacturers had a market share of over three percent in the month.</p>
<p>    Manufacturer	    Units/Share Jan 97 Units/Share Jan 96</p>
<p>    Volkswagen	8,306   18.7%	9,464   22.1%</p>
<p>    Peugeot-Citroen 6,178   13.9%	5,824   13.6%</p>
<p>    GM		  6,103   13.7%	4,297   10.0%</p>
<p>    Renault	   4,812   10.8%	5,250   12.2%</p>
<p>    Ford		3,161    7.1%	3,497    8.2%</p>
<p>    BMW		 2,869    6.5%	2,855    6.7%</p>
<p>    Mercedes-Benz   2,031    4.6%	2,008    4.7%</p>
<p>    Fiat		1,920    4.3%	1,816    4.2%</p>
<p>    Toyota	    1,915    4.3%	1,819    4.2%</p>
<p>    Nissan	    1,743    3.9%	1,250    2.9%</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
